            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is Sprouts protein powder healthy?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  Both house powders have short, reasonable labels: about 18 g of whey protein in 100 calories, or 20 g of pea and rice protein in about 120 calories, with no added sugar and natural sweeteners, per the labels. That makes them a fine snack or smoothie protein. People with kidney disease, pregnancy or medication should ask a doctor or registered dietitian first.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Sprouts protein powder contain stevia or artificial sweeteners?</h3></summary>
