            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Does Sprouts vegan protein powder contain dairy or gluten?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  No. Sprouts lists its vegan protein as vegan, dairy-free and gluten-free, built on pea protein isolate and organic brown rice protein. The Sprouts whey is milk-based and contains lactose, though it is also labeled gluten-free. The whey label notes it is made in a facility that processes egg, so check the allergen line for your needs.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Which Sprouts protein powder flavor is best?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  We have not tasted them. On the Sprouts shop, vanilla whey is the most reviewed house flavor, at 4.7 stars from a small number of buyers when we checked. For the vegan line, buyers generally find the chocolate and dessert-style flavors such as salted caramel easier to drink in water, and keep unflavored and mushroom blends for smoothies.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>

            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>What are the common complaints about Sprouts protein powder?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The most common complaints are price and protein per scoop. Small tubs work out to about $2 to $2.45 per 25 g, and the whey gives only about 18 g per scoop. With the vegan powder, buyers mention the usual plant-protein issues, a slightly gritty texture and a stevia aftertaste, and items are often out of stock online.
